8g9|a|	j:130v,61,6;175h,57,3;1n4i,54,33;1v8b,49,5;dk7,47,6;1bix,46,6;5ps,45,11;1v85,39,15;1ls9,39,5;17ng,38,5;gx2,27,5;1n4m,24,1;pwa,22,5;2966,17,5;16xg,8,2~1n4i,54,33;1v85,39,15;5ps,45,11;1bix,46,6;130v,61,6;dk7,47,6;gx2,27,5;pwa,22,5;17ng,38,5;2966,17,5;1v8b,49,5;1ls9,39,5;sle,4,4;175h,57,3;16xg,8,2
8gh|n|One of the seven colors into which the rays of light divide themselves, when refracted through a glass prism; the color of the clear sky, or a color resembling that, whether lighter or darker; a pigment having such color. Sometimes, poetically, the sky. ; A pedantic woman; a bluestocking. ; Low spirits; a fit of despondency; melancholy.	a:1h4n,80,1;i77,45,1;174w,28,2~174w,28,2;1h4n,80,1;i77,45,1	V:e7i,72,4~e7i,72,4	n:i77,45,1;96p,36,2;1q7u,35,2;2b2h,28,2~1q7u,35,2;96p,36,2;2b2h,28,2;i77,45,1	N:1h32,51,1;16mi,28,1;263t,9,1~16mi,28,1;263t,9,1;1h32,51,1
8gh|v|To make blue; to dye of a blue color; to make blue by heating, as metals, etc.	o:1kq1,3,1~1kq1,3,1
8gh|a|Having the color of the clear sky, or a hue resembling it, whether lighter or darker; as, the deep, blue sea; as blue as a sapphire; blue violets. ; Pale, without redness or glare, -- said of a flame; hence, of the color of burning brimstone, betokening the presence of ghosts or devils; as, the candle burns blue; the air was blue with oaths. ; Low in spirits; melancholy; as, to feel blue. ; Suited to produce low spirits; gloomy in prospect; as, thongs looked blue. ; Severe or over strict in morals; gloom; as, blue and sour religionists; suiting one who is over strict in morals; inculcating an impracticable, severe, or gloomy mortality; as, blue laws. ; Literary; -- applied to women; -- an abbreviation of bluestocking.	j:1h32,111,64;1h30,95,3;22me,91,10;22m8,85,123;div,69,7;4se,69,2;19bn,68,4;avz,55,1;1uh0,54,11;1say,50,2;16mi,48,4;174w,46,7;17ah,39,9;2b2h,34,3;2b2n,33,3~22m8,85,123;1h32,111,64;1uh0,54,11;22me,91,10;17ah,39,9;174w,46,7;div,69,7;179w,25,6;sem,4,5;1kq1,23,4;19bn,68,4;1f8s,29,4;16mi,48,4;jsl,23,4;263t,25,3
8hz|n|Full of blurs; blurred.	a:17j3,54,2~17j3,54,2
